WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.105
You've seen how a
basic RNN works.

2
00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:06.630
In this video, you learn about
the gated recurrent unit,

3
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.570
which has a modification
to the RNN hidden layer

4
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.220
that makes it much better at

5
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.515
capturing long-range
connections and helps

6
00:00:13.515 --> 00:00:16.200
a lot with the vanishing
gradient problems.

7
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.845
Let's take a look. You've
already seen the formula

8
00:00:19.845 --> 00:00:23.540
for computing the activations
at time t of an RNN.

9
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.920
It's the activation function
applied to the parameter W_a

10
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.960
times the activations for

11
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.280
a previous time
sediment the current

12
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.530
input and then plus the bias.

13
00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.225
I'm going to draw
this as a picture.

14
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:39.785
The RNN units I'm going
to draw as a picture,

15
00:00:39.785 --> 00:00:47.000
drawn as a box which
inputs a of t minus 1,

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.385
deactivation for the last
timestep and also inputs x^t,

17
00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:56.075
and these two go together,

18
00:00:56.075 --> 00:00:58.250
and after some weights

19
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.880
and after this type of
linear calculation,

20
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.945
if g is a tanh
activation function,

21
00:01:05.945 --> 00:01:07.780
then after the tanh,

22
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.830
it computes the output
of activation, a.

23
00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:18.500
The output activation a^t
might also be parsed to

24
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.400
say a softmax unit or
something that could then

25
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.440
be used to outputs y hat ^t.

26
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.190
This is maybe a visualization
of the RNN unit of

27
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:35.660
the hidden layer of the
RNN in terms of a picture.

28
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.010
I want to show you this picture

29
00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.900
because we're going to
use a similar picture to

30
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.470
explain the GRU or the
gated recurrent unit.

31
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.780
A lot of ideas of GRUs were due

32
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.750
to these two papers respectively

33
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.965
by Junyoung Chung,
Caglar, Gulcehre,

34
00:01:50.965 --> 00:01:54.015
KyungHyun Cho, and
Yoshua Bengio.

35
00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:56.315
Sometime is going to
refer to this sentence,

36
00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.920
which we'd seen in
the last video,

37
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.740
to motivate that given
a sentence like this,

38
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.630
you might need to
remember the cat was

39
00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:04.820
singular to make
sure you understand

40
00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.970
why that was rather than

41
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:11.535
were as of the cat was
for the cats were full.

42
00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:15.020
As we read in this sentence
from left to right,

43
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.790
the GRU unit is going to have
a new variable called C,

44
00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.540
which stands for cell,
for memory cell.

45
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.565
What the memory cell do is

46
00:02:25.565 --> 00:02:27.580
it will provide a bit of memory.

47
00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.275
Remember, for example,

48
00:02:29.275 --> 00:02:32.000
whether cat was
singular or plural,

49
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.670
so that when it gets much
further into the sentence,

50
00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.500
it can still work on

51
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.090
the consideration
whether the subject

52
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.505
of the sentence was
singular or plural.

53
00:02:40.505 --> 00:02:44.930
At time t, the memory cell
will have some value c of

54
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.670
t. What we'll see is
that the GRU unit will

55
00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.800
actually output an activation
value a of t that's

56
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.090
equal to c of t.
For now I wanted to

57
00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.935
use different symbols c and

58
00:02:57.935 --> 00:03:00.620
a to denote the
memory cell value and

59
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.690
the output activation value

60
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.640
even though they're
the same and I'm using

61
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.770
this notation because
when we talked about

62
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.065
LSTMs a little bit later,

63
00:03:09.065 --> 00:03:10.980
these will be two
different values.

64
00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.520
But for now, for the GRU c of t

65
00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.130
is equal to the output
activation a of

66
00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.460
t. These are the equations that

67
00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.750
govern the computations
of a GRU unit.

68
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.235
At every time step,

69
00:03:25.235 --> 00:03:27.710
we're going to consider
an overwriting

70
00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:31.770
the memory cell with a
value c tilde of t. This

71
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.370
going to be a candidate
for replacing c of

72
00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.320
t. We're going to compute

73
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.965
this using an
activation function,

74
00:03:38.965 --> 00:03:42.600
tanh of w_c,

75
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.830
and so that's the
parameter matrix w_c

76
00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.200
and we'll pass it as
parameter matrix.

77
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.990
The previous value of

78
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.090
the memory cell, the
activation value,

79
00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.045
as well as the current input

80
00:03:56.045 --> 00:03:59.265
value x^t and then plus a bias.

81
00:03:59.265 --> 00:04:00.830
C tilde of t is going to be

82
00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.800
a candidate for replacing c^t.

83
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:09.695
Then the key, really the
important idea of the GRU,

84
00:04:09.695 --> 00:04:12.230
it will be that
we'll have a gate.

85
00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.815
The gate I'm going
to call Gamma_u.

86
00:04:15.815 --> 00:04:19.920
This is the capital
Greek alphabet, Gamma_u,

87
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.030
and u stands for update gate.

88
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.910
This would be a value
between 0 and 1.

89
00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:31.835
To develop your intuition
about how GRUs work,

90
00:04:31.835 --> 00:04:36.560
think of Gamma_u this gate
value as being always 0 or 1.

91
00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.110
Although in practice,
your computer with

92
00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:43.185
a sigmoid function
applied to this.

93
00:04:43.185 --> 00:04:47.325
Remember that the sigmoid
function looks like this,

94
00:04:47.325 --> 00:04:51.150
as value is always
between 0 and 1.

95
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.020
For most of the possible
ranges of the input,

96
00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.670
the sigmoid function
is either very,

97
00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.180
very close to 0 or very,

98
00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.800
very close to 1.

99
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.890
For intuition, think of Gamma as

100
00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:05.320
being either 0 or 1
most of the time.

101
00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.070
I chose the alphabet
Gamma for this

102
00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.360
because if you look
at a gated fence,

103
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.290
it looks a bit like
this, I guess.

104
00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.330
Then there are a lot of
Gammas in this fence.

105
00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.070
That's why your
Gamma_u we're going to

106
00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.405
use to denote the gate.

107
00:05:23.405 --> 00:05:25.985
Also Greek alphabet G,

108
00:05:25.985 --> 00:05:29.630
like G for gate, so G for
Gamma and G for gate.

109
00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:35.839
Then next the key part of
the GRU is this equation,

110
00:05:35.839 --> 00:05:38.360
which is that we have come up

111
00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.355
with a candidate where
we're thinking of

112
00:05:40.355 --> 00:05:44.000
updating C using c tilde

113
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.800
and then the gate will decide

114
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.020
whether or not we
actually update it.

115
00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:53.525
The way to think about it
is maybe this memory cell C

116
00:05:53.525 --> 00:05:56.060
is going to be set to
either zero or one

117
00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.074
depending on whether the
word you're conserving,

118
00:05:59.074 --> 00:06:03.590
really the subject of the
sentence is singular or plural.

119
00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.930
Because it's singular,
let's say that we

120
00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.120
set this to one and
if it was plural,

121
00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.425
maybe we'll set this as a zero
and then the GRU unit will

122
00:06:12.425 --> 00:06:18.230
memorize the value of the
C^t all the way until here,

123
00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.500
where this is still
equal to one and

124
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.160
so that tells it was singular
so use the choice was.

125
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:28.655
The job of the gate, of gamma u,

126
00:06:28.655 --> 00:06:32.435
is to decide when do
you update this value.

127
00:06:32.435 --> 00:06:34.625
In particular, when you
see the phrase the cat,

128
00:06:34.625 --> 00:06:37.130
you know that you're talking
about a new concept,

129
00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.720
the subject of the sentence cat.

130
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.840
That would be a good time
to update this bit and then

131
00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:45.260
maybe when you're done
using it the cat was full,

132
00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.060
then you know I don't
need to memorize

133
00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.000
anymore I can just forget that.

134
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.790
The specific equation we'll use

135
00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.100
for the GRU is the following;

136
00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.580
which is that the actual
value of C^t would be

137
00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.300
equal to this gate times

138
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:07.820
the candidate value
plus one minus

139
00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:15.590
the gate times the old
value C^t minus one.

140
00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.875
Notice that if the gate,

141
00:07:18.875 --> 00:07:21.230
if this update value
of z equal to one,

142
00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.185
then is saying set
the new value of C^t

143
00:07:24.185 --> 00:07:27.410
equal to this candidate value
so that's like over here,

144
00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.045
set the gate equal to one

145
00:07:29.045 --> 00:07:31.310
so go ahead and update that bit.

146
00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.475
Then for all of these
values in the middle,

147
00:07:34.475 --> 00:07:36.320
you should have the gate equal

148
00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.200
zero so do the same,
don't update it,

149
00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.700
just hang on to the
old value because

150
00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.770
if gamma u is equal to zero,

151
00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.570
then this would be zero and

152
00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.925
this will be one and
so it's just setting

153
00:07:49.925 --> 00:07:52.550
C^t equal to the old value

154
00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.860
even as you scan the
sentence from left to right.

155
00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.360
When the gate is equal to

156
00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.565
zero as saying, don't update it,

157
00:07:58.565 --> 00:08:01.100
just hang on to the value
and don't forget what it's

158
00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.575
value was and so that way,

159
00:08:03.575 --> 00:08:05.435
even when you get all
the way down here,

160
00:08:05.435 --> 00:08:07.250
hopefully you've
just been setting

161
00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.140
C^t equal C^t minus one

162
00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:13.685
all along and still memorizes
the cat was singular.

163
00:08:13.685 --> 00:08:19.070
Let me also draw a picture
to denote the GRU unit.

164
00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.230
By the way, when you look in

165
00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.484
online blog posts and
textbooks and tutorials,

166
00:08:24.484 --> 00:08:27.320
these types of pictures are
quite popular for explaining

167
00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.115
GRUs as well as we'll
see later LSTM units.

168
00:08:31.115 --> 00:08:34.130
I personally find the equations
easier to understand in

169
00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:35.780
the pictures so if the picture

170
00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.580
doesn't make sense
don't worry about it,

171
00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:41.495
but I'll just draw it in
case it helps some of you.

172
00:08:41.495 --> 00:08:44.015
The GRU unit inputs

173
00:08:44.015 --> 00:08:46.280
C^t minus one for the
previous time step

174
00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.245
and this happens to be equal to

175
00:08:48.245 --> 00:08:51.350
80 minus one so it
takes us as input.

176
00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:55.010
Then it also takes
this input X^t.

177
00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.300
Then these two
things get combined

178
00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.580
together and with

179
00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.280
some appropriate waiting
and some tonnage.

180
00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.880
This gives you c tilde t,

181
00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.240
which is a candidate for
replacing C^t and then we have

182
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.920
a different set
of parameters and

183
00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.780
through a sigmoid
activation function,

184
00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.250
this gives you gamma u,

185
00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.130
which is the update
gate and then finally,

186
00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:21.170
all of these things combined

187
00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.945
together through
another operation.

188
00:09:23.945 --> 00:09:25.700
I won't write out
the formula but

189
00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.860
this box here which
are shaded in purple,

190
00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:31.520
represents this equation
which we had down there.

191
00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:35.344
That's what this purple
operation represents

192
00:09:35.344 --> 00:09:39.080
and it takes as input
the gate value,

193
00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.045
the candidate new value,

194
00:09:41.045 --> 00:09:43.010
that's the gate value again,

195
00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:46.970
and the old value for C^t
it takes as input this,

196
00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.685
this and this, and together they

197
00:09:49.685 --> 00:09:53.690
generate the new value
for the memory cell.

198
00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.015
That's C^t equals a.

199
00:09:56.015 --> 00:09:59.480
If you wish, you could also
use this impulses through

200
00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.630
a soft-max or something to make

201
00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:09.245
some prediction for Y^t
so that is the GRU units.

202
00:10:09.245 --> 00:10:11.660
These are slightly
simplified version of it.

203
00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.915
What is remarkably good
at is through the gate

204
00:10:14.915 --> 00:10:17.090
deciding that when you're

205
00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.830
scanning the sentence
from left to right,

206
00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.510
say that that's a
good time to update

207
00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.415
one to the memory
cell and enter,

208
00:10:22.415 --> 00:10:23.645
not change it,

209
00:10:23.645 --> 00:10:26.900
until you get to the point
where you really needed to use

210
00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:28.790
this memory cell that you

211
00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:31.145
had set even much
earlier in the sentence.

212
00:10:31.145 --> 00:10:36.650
Now, because the gate is quite

213
00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:39.020
easy to set to zero so long as

214
00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.960
this quantity is a
large negative value,

215
00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.790
then up to numerical round-off,

216
00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.475
the update gate will
be essentially zero,

217
00:10:46.475 --> 00:10:48.395
very close to zero.

218
00:10:48.395 --> 00:10:49.775
When that's the case,

219
00:10:49.775 --> 00:10:51.830
then this update
equation and sub

220
00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:56.450
setting C^t equals
C^t minus one and so

221
00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:59.855
this is very good at maintaining
the value for the cell

222
00:10:59.855 --> 00:11:04.310
and because gamma can
be so close to zero,

223
00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:10.010
can be 0.000001 or even
smaller than that.

224
00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.810
it doesn't suffer from much of

225
00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.610
a vanishing gradient
problem because

226
00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.635
in say gamma so close to zero

227
00:11:15.635 --> 00:11:19.850
that this becomes essentially
C^t equals C^t minus

228
00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:23.210
one and the value of C^t
is maintained pretty much

229
00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:27.350
exactly even across
many times that.

230
00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.060
This can help significantly

231
00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.920
with the vanishing
gradient problem

232
00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.990
and therefore allowing
your network to

233
00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.375
learn even very
long-range dependencies,

234
00:11:35.375 --> 00:11:38.150
such as the cat and
was are related

235
00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:39.440
even if they are separated by

236
00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.360
a lot of words in the middle.

237
00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.640
Now, I just want to talk over

238
00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.625
some more details of
how you implement this.

239
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:50.345
In the equations have written,

240
00:11:50.345 --> 00:11:53.195
C^t can be a vector.

241
00:11:53.195 --> 00:11:57.650
If you have 100-dimensional
hidden activation value,

242
00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.110
then C^t can be
100-dimensional Zai,

243
00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:04.400
and so C^t would also be
the same dimension and

244
00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.470
Gamma would also be

245
00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.030
the same dimension as

246
00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.010
the other things I'm
drawing in boxes.

247
00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.470
In that case, these asterisks

248
00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:16.355
are actually element-wise
multiplication.

249
00:12:16.355 --> 00:12:20.600
Here, if the gates

250
00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.820
is 100-dimensional
vector, what it is,

251
00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:27.665
is really 100-dimensional
vector of bits,

252
00:12:27.665 --> 00:12:30.110
the value is mostly 0 and 1,

253
00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:33.485
that tells you of this
100-dimensional memory cell,

